  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Traço Capturado",
    "overview": "The data of the author's thesis becomes the identity: a child's pre-writing finger stroke, recorded with speed and pressure, is what draws the site. The default world is a dark ink-navy capture screen; light theme is its paper-cool counterpart where the same stroke is drawn in ink. Everything the stroke touches is an academic, institutional page: the voice stays scholarly, never a toy, never a cold CV.\n\nOne idea carries the system: a short rounded stroke in the trace ramp (amber slow, pink mid, cyan fast) marks the start of things. It opens section titles, grows under a nav link, slides across a card's top edge, and is drawn full-width in the hero. Surfaces are flat and unboxed; hierarchy comes from type scale, that stroke, and 2px rules.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark ink-navy by default, light paper-cool counterpart; follows the OS, with a manual toggle.",
      "One three-stop trace ramp (slow, mid, fast), used only for strokes and state.",
      "Bricolage Grotesque display over Atkinson Hyperlegible Next body.",
      "Entries open with a stroke; no boxed cards, no shadows.",
      "AA contrast checked per token pair; 44px minimum targets; reduced motion shows a static trace."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Trace Ramp Rule",
        "body": "The three trace colors appear only as strokes, gradients of strokes, and state (hover, pressed, selection, the primary action). They never fill panels or color body text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paired Theme Rule",
        "body": "Every color is a theme pair. Never use a dark value on paper or the reverse; the light trace colors are darkened specifically to hold 5:1 or better on paper-cool.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Display face for headings, names, and the call line; Atkinson for everything read at length. Do not set paragraphs in the display face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-By-Default Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces stay flat; separation is a 2px rule or whitespace. A hovering card extends its stroke, it does not rise.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do open sections and entries with a short rounded stroke in the trace ramp.",
      "Do keep every state change (hover, current, pressed) as a stroke growing or a border turning amber.",
      "Do set min 44px targets and 3px focus rings; verify 5:1 on UI boundaries and 4.5:1 on text per theme.",
      "Do read all colors from the theme custom properties so light, dark and manual toggle stay in sync.",
      "Do pair every motion with a reduced-motion static equivalent."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use the trace colors as panel fills or for paragraph text.",
      "Don't box entries in cards with shadows or filled backgrounds; the open entry with a top rule is the form.",
      "Don't use one theme's trace values in the other theme.",
      "Don't make the trace carry information; it is illustrative and must stay aria-hidden.",
      "Don't drift toward a childish toy look (primary-color blobs, rounded cartoon type) or a cold institutional CV page; the stroke is the identity, the voice stays academic."
    ]
  }
}